    <Investigation>
        <name>Firefly Aerospace's Blue Ghost Mission 1</name>
        <type>Mission</type>
        <start_date>2025-01-15</start_date>
        <stop_date>2025-03-16</stop_date>
        <description>
            As part of NASA’s CLPS (Commercial Lunar Payload Services) initiative and Artemis campaign, Firefly’s Blue Ghost lunar lander 
            delivered ten NASA science and technology instruments to Mare Crisium on the near side of the Moon. The CLPS name for the delivery 
            is CLPS Task Order (TO) 19D and the Firefly Aerospace mission name is Blue Ghost Mission 1. Blue Ghost Mission 1 (BGM1) launched on 
            Jan 15, 2025 and landed on March 2, 2025. The surface mission extended through one lunar day and multiple hours into the lunar night 
            before concluding on March 16, 2025.
        </description>
    </Investigation>
